The VMS community loves to tell the tale of the Irish National Railway's
VMScluster and its 17-year uptime record. Tru64 UNIX and its Alpha
precursors haven't been around for 17 years, but perhaps you have a
TruCluster record worthy of Bragging Rights. If so, you might want to visit
http://www.compaq-unixgames.com/ and register for the Unix Games.

Once you've registered for the Games, go to

http://www.compaq-unixgames.com/htmlv/f-welcome.htm

scroll down to the bottom of the page and click on the "Cluster Conquerors
Contest"

You can then summarize your exploits in any of six categories including:
Highest Performance TruCluster System, Highest Cost of Downtime, Most
Unusual Location, Longest Duration of Uptime, Most Nodes, and Most Storage.
Swell Prizes are available for winning entries.

The rules:
Your cluster has to be on a Compaq Tru64 UNIX server
You may submit more than one cluster, but each unique cluster may be
submitted to only one category
Stories are limited to 500 words, but can include a schematic drawing
All submissions are due 28 February 2001
The registration form must be filled out completely
You can send a photo of you and your cluster for posting


--
