You haven't provided enough information for a detailed response.

maxuprc is the maximum number of processes that a given UID (user)
can start.  In the oldest versions of Tru64 UNIX, Digital UNIX or
DEC OSF/1, this is a parameter in the system configuration file.
To change it, edit the configuration, change the value to something
higher, rebuild the kernel, copy the new kernel to the root and
reboot.  Systems with a tuning guide or system admin. guide chapter
on the configuration file should describe how to do this in more
detail.

Recent versions of Digital UNIX and Tru64 UNIX (V4 and later)
put this parameter in sysconfigtab.  See the sysconfig or
dxkerneltuner manual pages for information on how to change
parameters.  Very recent versions have manual pages that
describe the different tunable parameters; sys_attrs_"subsys".
You probably want sys_attrs_proc.

